@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-inspectors`
IMPORT `g5-senior-inspector`
IMPORT `g5-testing-bodies`
IMPORT `g5-test-conduct`
IMPORT `g5-withdrawal`

-- g5-tests-red.l4: assertions that are MEANT TO FAIL, and are counted.
-- Each one asserts, of the function that takes the reading CHOSEN in a fork, the answer the REJECTED reading gives.
-- So each fails while the encoding takes the chosen reading, which is the proof that the fork matters and that this
-- harness can fail.  The alternative reading's own function is tested, and passes, in the tests module of its
-- section.  There are 19 assertions below and all 19 are expected to fail: `check.sh` lists the count as expected.
-- (The forks F-DUTY and F-ACTOR concern DEONTIC values, which cannot be asserted; their traces are in the tests
-- modules of the sections.)

§ `Assertions that must fail: the rejected readings against the readings taken`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an inspector who is fully equipped` MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST `enter a place to supervise`, `require information or a document`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown` MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST `enter a place to supervise`, `require information or a document`), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`an inspector with no badge in sight` MEANS
    `An inspector at work` OF TRUE, (LIST `enter a place to supervise`, `require information or a document`), TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a demand for a document` MEANS `Demand under section 31(2)` OF TRUE, `a document that is not computer output`, TRUE, TRUE
`a disciplinary convict the Minister finds unfit` MEANS
    `Candidate for authorisation as an inspector` OF TRUE, (`Record of offences` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE), TRUE, TRUE, NOTHING
`a direction of 30 days` MEANS `a number of days directed for keeping` 30
`a calendar with 31 January 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 1 31)
`an employee authorised only to test` MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a qualifying corporation that is not yet a testing body` MEANS
    `Corporation that would serve as a testing body` OF TRUE, TRUE, (`Person connected with a testing body` OF (`Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF (`Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), FALSE), (EMPTY), TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE
`a person under investigation for a disqualifying offence` MEANS
    `Standing as to offences (ss 35 and 36)` OF (`Record of offences` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE), FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`a change as to work procedures after a hearing` MEANS
    `Change under section 36(d)` OF `a condition or instruction as to work procedures`, TRUE
`an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` MEANS
    `Instrument of authorisation under section 36(e)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (JUST (`a number of days fixed in the instrument` 30))
`an entry after the holder withdrew his consent` MEANS
    `Entry by a tester or an expert under section 37` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a tester doing an auxiliary test` MEANS `Tester or expert at work` OF `acting as a tester`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`an unpublished checklist` MEANS `Checklist used by a tester or an expert` OF TRUE, FALSE
`a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026` MEANS `Suspension under section 39(a)` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (`a number of days fixed by the Minister` 30)
`a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` MEANS
    `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, (JUST (`Demand under section 39(b)` OF (YMD 2026 3 2), (`a number of days fixed by the Minister` 14))), FALSE, FALSE
`a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (LIST YMD 2026 3 16)
`a calendar with no rest days` MEANS `Calendar of rest days` OF (EMPTY)
`a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` MEANS
    `Case for revoking or suspending an authorisation` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE
`an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026` MEANS
    `Authorisation of a tester or an expert as recorded` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31), (JUST (YMD 2026 6 15)), (EMPTY)

§§ `The 19 assertions that fail`

-- 1. F-DEMAND: reading A (certificate need only be held) says an inspector who refused to show it, when asked, may still use his powers.
#ASSERT `s 32 — the inspector may use the powers` `an inspector whose certificate was demanded and not shown`
-- 2. F-ITEM7: the alternative says a demand by an inspector without a badge is still a document demanded under s.31(2).
#ASSERT `the inspector's demand for a document under s.31(2) was lawfully made` `an inspector with no badge in sight` `a demand for a document`
-- 3. F-OFFENCE: the alternative counts a disciplinary conviction, so this candidate may not be authorised.
#ASSERT NOT `s 30(b)(1) — the candidate was not convicted of an offence that makes him unfit, in the Minister's opinion` `a disciplinary convict the Minister finds unfit`
-- 4. F-P22: the alternative applies s.10(c) to the retention period and ends it on 1 February.
#ASSERT `s 31(4) — the last day of the period for keeping directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `a direction of 30 days` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
-- 5. F-START (P22): the alternative begins keeping the day after the direction.
#ASSERT NOT `s 31(4) — keeping is directed on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `for a direction given on` (YMD 2026 1 1) `and a period of` `a direction of 30 days`
-- 6. F-OVERLAP: the alternative keeps an employee authorised only to test out of the experts.
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised only to test`
-- 7. F-LOOP: read strictly, s.35(3) cannot be met by a corporation that is not yet a testing body.
#ASSERT NOT `s 35(3) — the corporation proved to the Minister's satisfaction that it employs testers in the fields and to the extent required` `a qualifying corporation that is not yet a testing body`
-- 8. F-PROCEEDING: the broader reading counts a criminal investigation as a pending proceeding.
#ASSERT `s 35(2) — the person was convicted of a disqualifying offence, or a criminal proceeding is pending on suspicion of one` `a person under investigation for a disqualifying offence`
-- 9. F-CHANGE: reading B lets the Minister change a work-procedures condition after a hearing.
#ASSERT `s 36(d) — the change may be made: it concerns modes of action, and the tester or expert was given an opportunity to argue in writing` `a change as to work procedures after a hearing`
-- 10. F-P23: the alternative applies s.10(c) to the authorisation and ends it on 1 February.
#ASSERT `s 36(e) — the last day of the authorisation` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
-- 11. F-START (P23): the alternative begins the authorisation the day after it was granted.
#ASSERT NOT `s 36(e) — the authorisation runs on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `under` `an instrument of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
-- 12. F-WITHDRAW: the alternative ignores a withdrawal of consent.
#ASSERT `s 37(b)(2) — the holder gave written consent to the entry, and it stands` `an entry after the holder withdrew his consent`
-- 13. F-PUBLISH: the alternative makes publication a condition of using the checklist.
#ASSERT NOT `s 37(a)(3) — the tester or expert may use the checklist` `a tester doing an auxiliary test` `an unpublished checklist`
-- 14. F-P24: the alternative applies s.10(c) to the suspension and ends it on 1 February.
#ASSERT `s 39(a) — the last day of a suspension` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 2 1
-- 15. F-START (P24): the alternative begins the suspension the day after it began.
#ASSERT NOT `s 39(a) — the authorisation is suspended on the day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `by` `a suspension of 30 days from 1 January 2026`
-- 16. F-P25: the alternative does NOT apply s.10(c) to the time directed, so a decision on 17 March is allowed even with 16 March a rest day.
#ASSERT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition, demand of 2 March for 14 days, not met` (YMD 2026 3 17) `a calendar with Monday 16 March 2026 a rest day`
-- 17. F-STATUS-DAY: the alternative lets a revocation take effect the day after it is made.
#ASSERT `s 36(e), s 39 — the authorisation is in force on the day` (YMD 2026 6 15) `an authorisation revoked on 15 June 2026`
-- 18. F-DISCLOSE: the literal reading says a disclosure the Law itself requires (the hand-over of s.38(b)) is not permitted.
#ASSERT NOT `s 38(c) — the disclosure or use is permitted` FALSE TRUE
-- 19. F-GROUNDS: the stricter reading applies the cure-first rule to a lapsed condition even beside another ground, so he may not act yet.
#ASSERT NOT `s 39 — the Minister may revoke or suspend the authorisation` `a lapsed condition and a poor professional level, no demand` (YMD 2026 3 1) `a calendar with no rest days`
